WEBVTT

1
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.708


2
00:00:46.708 --> 00:00:51.833
<b>Here, Lord Krishna is elaborating on</b>
<b>what was said in the previous verses.</b>

3
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:54.541
<b>He states that the soul is eternal,</b>

4
00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:56.541
<b>indestructible.</b>

5
00:00:56.541 --> 00:01:01.791
<b>What perishes is only this body,</b>
<b>which is material</b>

6
00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:03.500
<b>merely a house</b>

7
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.791
<b>where the soul dwells temporarily.</b>

8
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.666


9
00:01:12.666 --> 00:01:18.125
<b>Lord Krishna says that which pervades this</b>
<b>entire body is indestructible.</b>

10
00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:20.875
<b>What pervades this entire body?</b>

11
00:01:20.875 --> 00:01:22.375
<b>Our consciousness,</b>

12
00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:25.875
<b>and this consciousness comes from our soul.</b>

13
00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:29.125
<b>It is the soul that is indestructible.</b>

14
00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:31.791
<b>In the next verse, He also explains</b>

15
00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:37.666
<b>that this body is merely a worldly dwelling</b>
<b>for this eternal soul.</b>

16
00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:40.916
<b>The destruction of this body is certain.</b>

17
00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:44.500
<b>Here, He is refuting Arjuna's notion</b>

18
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.416
<b>where Arjuna thinks</b>

19
00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:51.000
<b>that by not fighting this war,</b>
<b>his kinsmen will be saved from death.</b>

20
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.583
<b>But this is not possible.</b>

21
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:58.916
<b>Death will not be averted by Arjuna's decision</b>
<b>to fight or not to fight.</b>

22
00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:03.958
<b>Krishna is trying to make Arjuna understand</b>
<b>from both perspectives.</b>

23
00:02:03.958 --> 00:02:07.041
<b>The kinsmen Arjuna is grieving for</b>

24
00:02:07.041 --> 00:02:10.291
<b>their bodies are destined to perish,</b>

25
00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:13.416
<b>whether in war or not.</b>

26
00:02:13.416 --> 00:02:15.916
<b>So what is there to grieve about?</b>

27
00:02:15.916 --> 00:02:18.833
<b>Moreover, whether death comes</b>
<b>today or tomorrow,</b>

28
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:22.625
<b>their soul exists today and</b>
<b>will remain tomorrow, </b>

29
00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:24.291
<b>never to die.</b>

30
00:02:24.291 --> 00:02:25.291
<b>So here again,</b>

31
00:02:25.291 --> 00:02:31.500
<b>how can there be grief for that</b>
<b>which cannot be destroyed?</b>

32
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.875
<b>He wants to say</b>

33
00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:33.833
<b>Arjuna,</b>

34
00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:36.791
<b>in both these conditions, grief is futile.</b>

35
00:02:36.791 --> 00:02:42.291
<b>You should free yourself from this illusion and</b>
<b>simply perform your duty,</b>

36
00:02:42.291 --> 00:02:45.208
<b>enter the battlefield.</b>

37
00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:50.125


38
00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:52.833
<b>When we wear clothes,</b>

39
00:02:52.833 --> 00:02:59.625
<b>they move according to our body's movements.</b>

40
00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:00.416
<b>But</b>

41
00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:04.250
<b>the moment we take off these clothes,</b>

42
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:15.166
<b>remove our body from them,</b>
<b>they lie lifeless on the ground, merely a heap.</b>

43
00:03:15.166 --> 00:03:16.583
<b>So</b>

44
00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:21.250
<b>what gives movement to the clothes?</b>

45
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.250
<b>Our body.</b>

46
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:28.291
<b>Do the clothes have any power of their own?</b>

47
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.333
<b>No, they don't.</b>

48
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:31.875
<b>Similarly,</b>

49
00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:36.083
<b>this body is merely a garment for the soul.</b>

50
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:40.875
<b>This body has no consciousness of its own;</b>

51
00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:46.625
<b>whatever exists is a gift</b>
<b>of the soul dwelling within.</b>

52
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:48.250
<b>A day will come</b>

53
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.250
<b>when the soul will remove this garment,</b>

54
00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.375
<b>will exit from it,</b>

55
00:03:54.375 --> 00:04:01.541
<b>and then this body too will lie like</b>
<b>a lifeless heap of clothes.</b>

56
00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.583
<b>Tell me something</b>

57
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:06.916
<b>are you a servant to your clothes?</b>

58
00:04:06.916 --> 00:04:08.125
<b>No, right?</b>

59
00:04:08.125 --> 00:04:14.958
<b>Do you spend your entire life according to</b>
<b>the clothes you wear?</b>

60
00:04:14.958 --> 00:04:16.375
<b>No, right?</b>

61
00:04:16.375 --> 00:04:19.500
<b>Similarly,</b>

62
00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:28.625
<b>isn't it wrong to live life solely influenced</b>
<b>by this body-like garment?</b>

63
00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:33.125
<b>Have you ever thought about this?</b>

64
00:04:33.125 --> 00:04:42.708
<b>Live life inspired by the soul that provides</b>
<b>consciousness to this body, by its awareness.</b>

65
00:04:42.708 --> 00:04:46.958
<b>Living life with consciousness means</b>
<b>staying aware.</b>

66
00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:51.250
<b>Not just working like a machine,</b>

67
00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.875
<b>but being thoughtful in every action.</b>

68
00:04:54.875 --> 00:04:59.291
<b>Having the ability to question your desires.</b>

69
00:04:59.291 --> 00:05:04.958
<b>Taking complete responsibility for</b>
<b>your actions and thoughts.</b>

70
00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:09.791
<b>A machine does none of this</b>

71
00:05:09.791 --> 00:05:14.208
<b>it will follow whatever instructions it's given,</b>

72
00:05:14.208 --> 00:05:15.916
<b>right or wrong,</b>

73
00:05:15.916 --> 00:05:17.708
<b>good or bad,</b>

74
00:05:17.708 --> 00:05:25.041
<b>won't question itself, won't take responsibility</b>
<b>for any consequences.</b>

75
00:05:25.041 --> 00:05:29.000
<b>You're not like that, are you?</b>

76
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.708
<b>Know your consciousness,</b>

77
00:05:31.708 --> 00:05:33.416
<b>develop it.</b>

78
00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:39.833
<b>Such a life is the mark of</b>
<b>a spiritually awakened person.</b>

79
00:05:40.458 --> 00:05:44.291


80
00:05:44.291 --> 00:05:48.375
<b>No matter how deeply we love someone,</b>

81
00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:53.208
<b>one day they will part from us.</b>

82
00:05:53.208 --> 00:05:56.541
<b>Either circumstances will separate us,</b>

83
00:05:56.541 --> 00:06:00.250
<b>or death will.</b>

84
00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.416
<b>Death cannot be averted,</b>

85
00:06:03.416 --> 00:06:09.541
<b>and this mortal body's end is certain.</b>

86
00:06:09.541 --> 00:06:10.958
<b>But</b>

87
00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:17.708
<b>knowing this certainty, we cannot abandon</b>
<b>everything in distress.</b>

88
00:06:17.708 --> 00:06:22.333
<b>We must continue performing our</b>
<b>duties in every situation.</b>

89
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:23.583
<b>Yes,</b>

90
00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:29.041
<b>the death of a loved one is extremely painful.</b>

91
00:06:29.041 --> 00:06:30.291
<b>And</b>

92
00:06:30.291 --> 00:06:35.000
<b> this is where we need to understand</b>
<b>the teachings of the Gita,</b>

93
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:40.708
<b>to follow this wisdom in our lives.</b>

94
00:06:40.708 --> 00:06:49.625
<b>Doing so won't eliminate the pain,</b>
<b>but it will certainly diminish it.</b>

95
00:06:49.625 --> 00:06:53.541
<b>Try understanding it this way.</b>

96
00:06:53.541 --> 00:06:58.333
<b>If you're meeting a dear friend for a limited time,</b>

97
00:06:58.333 --> 00:07:01.625
<b>would you spend every moment in sorrow? </b>

98
00:07:01.625 --> 00:07:03.083
<b>Because you know that</b>

99
00:07:03.083 --> 00:07:06.958
<b>period will end, they will leave?</b>

100
00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:08.750
<b>No, right?</b>

101
00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.750
<b>You will live each moment with love.</b>

102
00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:16.583
<b>And after they're gone, though there</b>
<b>will be some sadness,</b>

103
00:07:16.583 --> 00:07:21.166
<b>you won't sink into deep grief,</b>

104
00:07:21.166 --> 00:07:22.916
<b>because you know</b>

105
00:07:22.916 --> 00:07:27.666
<b>your friend is still well.</b>

106
00:07:27.666 --> 00:07:30.750
<b>Think for a moment</b>

107
00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:37.541
<b>even after death, our loved ones,</b>
<b>in their soul form, are still well.</b>

108
00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:42.666
<b>Try to adopt such a perspective in life.</b>

109
00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:47.541


110
00:07:47.541 --> 00:07:52.458
<b>Here we're discussing the</b>
<b>permanent and the perishable.</b>

111
00:07:52.458 --> 00:07:55.291
<b>The eternal and the momentary.</b>

112
00:07:55.291 --> 00:07:58.833
<b>What is eternal is truth, is right.</b>

113
00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:00.333
<b>What is momentary</b>

114
00:08:00.333 --> 00:08:04.333
<b>worrying about it is futile.</b>

115
00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:09.375
<b>Look at professional life</b>
<b>once from this perspective.</b>

116
00:08:09.375 --> 00:08:16.875
<b>How often does it happen that for</b>
<b>momentary gain, people forget their principles?</b>

117
00:08:16.875 --> 00:08:26.500
<b>Is it wise to forget principles that stand by us</b>
<b>forever, for something that's merely temporary?</b>

118
00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.833
<b>No, it's not.</b>

119
00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:34.791
<b>If we understand well that worldly things</b>
<b>are temporary by nature,</b>

120
00:08:34.791 --> 00:08:36.083
<b>here today</b>

121
00:08:36.083 --> 00:08:37.208
<b>and gone tomorrow,</b>

122
00:08:37.208 --> 00:08:46.041
<b>then we won't risk our moral</b>
<b>principles for these things.</b>

123
00:08:46.041 --> 00:08:50.166
<b>If we understand our eternal nature as souls,</b>

124
00:08:50.166 --> 00:08:55.875
<b>we'll become more vigilant about our duties,</b>

125
00:08:55.875 --> 00:09:01.375
<b>because then we'll know that</b>
<b>this life isn't everything.</b>

126
00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:07.375
<b>The account of our good and bad deeds</b>
<b>will remain even after this life.</b>

127
00:09:07.375 --> 00:09:10.833
<b>This awareness will guide us</b>
<b>not just in personal life,</b>

128
00:09:10.833 --> 00:09:12.166
<b>but</b>

129
00:09:12.166 --> 00:09:15.166
<b>in professional life as well.</b>

